<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">archmage</ansi>

The Archmage is the elite class of the Arcanist (neutral wizard route). It
asks no alignment at level 30. It is the strongest reliable damage in the
game: the same spells, cast harder, faster and cheaper.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Overchannel       once every 4 rounds, a damage spell it casts deals 50%
                       more damage for 50% more mana
  35 Quick casting     damage spells chant one round less
  40 Thrifty casting   spells cost 15% less mana in all
  45 Arcane Barrage    Magic Missile strikes a second foe at full damage
  50 Frequent Overchannel   Overchannel every 3 rounds
  55 Steady casting    blows break its chant 50% less often in all
  60 Archmage's Storm  once a battle, a Shower of Sparks deals double damage
                       to every foe in the group, at no extra mana

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How it plays</ansi>

Everything is automatic. An Archmage casts as any wizard does (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>);
Overchannel and the Storm swell a cast that was coming anyway, and the line
says so: (overchannel, +50% damage, 9 mana) or (archmage's storm, double damage).
Overchannel is skipped when the extra mana would leave the Archmage short, and
the Storm is its first Shower of Sparks.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Wizard elite talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Deep Reserves, Focused Will, Spell
Edge. See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help wizard-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>.
